ved entirely  to the stage alongside several other  creative endeavors like furniture making  and writing  in particular cobb has spent the last  several years working on and touring  with his show americanmoore  based on an uncomfortable audition for  shakespeare play the show presents  cobb's dissection of the issue of race  and theater  americanmoore features him as an actor  auditioning for the title role in  othello all while the unseen director  pushes back against the performance  the first reading took place in 2013 and  he since toured the country with it  including an off-broadway run in 2019.  the show's message  resonates in unexpected ways a 16 year  old jewish girl  she gets up and says that's my story  robert duncan mcneil started his career  with small sci-fi guest spots in the 80s  before landing his first big role in  1992  cadet nicholas locarno on the star trek  the next generation episode the first  duty  three years later he landed the gig that  defined him tom paris on star trek  voyager  after that show wrapped up after seven  seasons in 2001 mcneil made a few tv  guest appearances before phasing out of  acting entirely  he hasn't disappeared though like his  voyager co-star roxanne dawson he's just  moved behind the camera  mcneil had wanted to direct before  voyager but his shows kept getting  cancelled before he had the opportunity  as he revealed to star trek.com on the  first day of the voyager pilot he  approached producer rick berman to make  it clear that he wanted to direct an  episode as soon as possible he then  started shadowing other trek directors  while spending time in edit bays and  screenings with berman  the first episode mcneal directed was  season 3's sacred ground  he went on to direct three more episodes  of voyager as well as four episodes of  star trek enterprise  he's since gone on to direct a variety  of other shows including everything from  desperate housewives to supernatural  carrie hand played little newt the  