ll ribcage the store  lives by the motto  the alphabet starts at d i remember  thinking i look  matronly and um  and like a stripper at the same time  goldstein started by importing high-end  bras from europe and her business grew  so much that she now has five stores in  two states  in 2016 she told cnbc that she was on  pace for 1.7 million dollars in sales  that year and that she was now more  recognized around los angeles as the  brawl lady rather than an actress  terry farrell played jadzia dax on star  trek deep space nine  for six seasons before getting killed  off reportedly after producer rick  berman refused to let her have a lighter  workload she then moved on to the cbs  sitcom becker and appeared in a few  movies but then stopped acting on screen  altogether after 2003 as she chose to  focus on her family  soon after her time on becker she moved  to hershey pennsylvania to raise her son  with her then husband brian baker  best known as the trench coat wearing  salesman in early 2000s sprint  commercials  she wanted stability for her son after  watching her own mother go through a few  divorces and she also wanted to commit  to raising him full time  outside of family time farrell found  other pursuits to keep herself grounded  she became a yoga instructor logging the  requisite 200 hours and teaching in  class at her local rec center in 2009  she and baker starred in a play together  at a local playhouse which  was the sum total of her acting for  years what's good about the intimacy  here is it's not really that different  when  a crew is all around you and you're  working in 2011 farrell told star  trek.com that she had retired from  acting but in 2017 she came out of  retirement to appear in the fan film  star trek renegades  anthony simcoe was a human behind dargo  fanscape's luxon warrior  playing the role from 1999 to 2004 the  six-foot five-inch australian combined  his intimidating figure with a natural  charm to become one of the most  memorable characters on the series  the heavy prosthetics that he wore meant  that he could have had a long career  post-farscape without getting typecast  but instead he spent a few years taking  on smaller roles before leaving acting  altogether  simcoe's twitter page describes him as a  former actor after he retired he started  simcoe consulting a global firm that  teaches business communication  companies across the world hire him to  help them with professional training as  he employs skills he learned during his  time acting  during a 2018 appearance on the punching  sideways podcast he noted  i've got a real passion for helping  people get along i'm one of those lucky  people who found their thing  in addition to consulting simcoe is also  a doctoral student studying storytelling  and machine learning  sabrina lloyd gained sci-fi fame in the  90s as wade one of the original lead  characters on the show sliders  the same decade she also had a lead role  in the decidedly not sci-fi show sports  night  her acting workload slowed down in the  new millennium with her only notable  role coming in the cbs series numbers  before fizzling out entirely  lloyd had settled in new york during her  acting career with her future husband  who was working at the united nations at  the time  one day he proposed marriage and  suggested that they moved to africa to  which she enthusiastically agreed  as lloyd revealed on the design mom blog  when people ask how she could give up  such a successful career her response is  how could i not i knew the acting world  so well i knew the streets of my city so  well  and here was the love of my life  stretching out his hands saying let's go  see the world  the couple ended up moving around the  world together including stops in uganda  where lloyd adopted one child and rome  where she gave birth to another  they're now primarily based in kenya  while also spending part of their time  in vancouver  jake lloyd was a rising child star when  he played anakin skywalker in star wars  episode 1 the phantom menace in 1999.  it's hard to imagine a role with higher  expectations in movie history  alas the negative response to his  performance fed into issues that led to  his retirement from acting  he quit around 2001 though he continued  to make the odd convention appearance  in 2012 he made it clear in an interview  with the sun that his disillusionment  with acting could be traced directly to  star wars as he put it  my entire school life was really a  living hell and i had to do up to 60  interviews a day  lloyd also blamed george lucas in  particular and destroyed every piece of  star wars memorabilia he owned  then in 2015 after lloyd physically  assaulted his mother she confirmed to  tmz that he was diagnosed with  schizophrenia when he was 19.  later that year he was arrested for  reckless driving driving without a  license and resisting  arrest he was moved to a psychiatric  facility while awaiting trial and his  family issued a statement in january  2020 saying that he had made progress  with his mental health struggles  randy ledvert started her career as a  penthouse pet but then she headed to  acting school  her first movie role was a small part in  1993's demolition man  and then several years later she had a  major part in season two of sci-fi as  the invisible man  but the most notable role of her career  was the android doyle in season 5 of  andromeda which lasted from 2004 to 2005  but her acting work dried up soon after  that due partly to motherhood but far  more to addiction  ledford started smoking marijuana at age  11 and by 14 she was regularly doing  coke and drinking alcohol  she spent almost all of her modeling  days doing uppers and downers to keep  herself going  she would stay clean while shooting but  party too much after work  having a child kept her clean for a few  years but her old habits eventually  destroyed her marriage and her  relationship with her son  she also stopped acting altogether after  a mental health incident forced her into  rehab she started getting her life back  together  she also had what she's called a miracle  baby at the age of 44.  ledford has been sober since 2012 and  regularly shares her story of addiction  to help others  she has unofficially retired and with a  story like hers a comeback can't be  ruled out  if you or anyone you know is struggling  with addiction issues help is available  be sure to reach out to the substance  abuse and mental health services  administration  samsa at 1-800-662-help  4357

